-# What you build out of the pool. Sets played as something other than normal
-# limited get their own text - Commander Legends: Battle for Baldur's Gate ran
-# its prerelease as a Commander Draft of the packs, not as sealed at all.
- case limited_format.play_variant
- when "commander"
  %p
    You don't open these as a sealed pool - the draft boosters are drafted,
    as a Commander Draft.
  = render "commander_draft_rules", limited_format: limited_format
- when "multiplayer"
  %p
    From cards you open and any number of basic land cards, build a 40 card deck.
  %p
    Games are played as free-for-all multiplayer, and you can attack multiple players.
- when "jumpstart"
  %p
    Every Jumpstart booster is a 20 card half deck built around a theme, with
    its own basic lands. Shuffle the two packs together and that is your 40
    card deck - there is no deck construction, and no lands to add.
  %p
    Jumpstart packs are interchangeable, so a pack of this set can be shuffled
    together with a pack of any other Jumpstart set instead.
- when "two-headed-giant"
  %p
    You open these packs in a team of two, and they are what your team gets
    between the two of you. From the cards you open and any number of basic land
    cards, each of you builds their own 40 card deck. Cards you don't use are a
    shared sideboard.
  = render "two_headed_giant_play"
- else
  %p
    From cards you open and any number of basic land cards, build a 40 card deck.
